<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:00Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>German economy frets about Saxony-Anhalt election results</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf6133afcf34e9e813de83e4921f8d71c297858799b9f264a465fb812bb717a6</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T18:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-economy-frets-about-saxony-anhalt-election-results/a-79162871--94d137604c23.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-economy-frets-about-saxony-anhalt-election-results/a-79162871?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD won the election in the eastern German state by a wide margin. While politicians and election analysts are still debating the reasons for the far-right party's popularity, economists are sounding the alarm.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>German police arrest suspect in power grid sabotage case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a484dee59cc0cf0131d1dc1ae1287725e83a8e5441de400d53ad29e3fb72b0e1</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T10:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-police-arrest-suspect-in-power-grid-sabotage-case/a-79161142--0b56d3da8acf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-police-arrest-suspect-in-power-grid-sabotage-case/a-79161142?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Investigators say the suspect used homemade rockets and conductive wire to target high-voltage lines in three German states, apparently as part of a campaign against fossil fuels.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Merkel's 'heart bleeds' after AfD win in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2a848534ebfedb3806641e19e091a0e52376ebc2fe43820ac418a891a1c0b55f</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/merkel-s-heart-bleeds-after-afd-win-in-saxony-anhalt/live-79153944--5083aaccea19.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/merkel-s-heart-bleeds-after-afd-win-in-saxony-anhalt/live-79153944?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former Chancellor Angela Merkel called the results in Saxony-Anhalt "simply shocking," and warned of the dangers of feelings trumping facts. The latest PISA education test scores also have Germany reeling.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt: Germany wakes up to 'unsettling' AfD victory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:33573291927fb91c2f03de780327209aa2e97d445c30a9d69c52ea931acc7d4c</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-germany-wakes-up-to-unsettling-afd-victory/live-78754934--2d9595de9f5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-germany-wakes-up-to-unsettling-afd-victory/live-78754934?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) party won the Saxony-Anhalt state election but without an absolute majority in parliament. Other European nations were wrestling with the impact of the results. Follow DW.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia announces it is closing Germany's consulate in St. Petersburg</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4dc98c1a67a41754ff67886fadafd1d5542aa4c102bad5a14b73986ac6a59915</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-announces-it-is-closing-germany-s-consulate-in-st-petersburg/a-79149908--0c758ae8cdb6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-announces-it-is-closing-germany-s-consulate-in-st-petersburg/a-79149908?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The tit-for-tat reaction comes after Germany said it is shutting down Russia's consulate in Bonn and its cultural center in Berlin.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>BSW and AfD – a political love-hate relationship in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a11682e391b096ddf6acd033994121926b2506602db2085d2a117531b5d76ad0</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T13:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bsw-and-afd-a-political-love-hate-relationship-in-germany/a-79185782--2f6a7962abcf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bsw-and-afd-a-political-love-hate-relationship-in-germany/a-79185782?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Sahra Wagenknecht Alliance (BSW) could help the Alternative for Germany (AfD) into power in Saxony-Anhalt. But the BSW is riddled with infighting</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Elversberg: Bundesliga newcomers from tiny town make waves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e1008e513888d9b989db3dbc70cc7058483d779cfedd92bb0f166d4c67592fe</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483--9d72d35ebb6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A team from a small southwestern German town of just 7,000 inhabitants made history by sealing promotion to become the 59th club to play in the Bundesliga. Elversberg has got off to a memorable start.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Nicaragua challenges German arms exports to Israel at ICJ</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b9fb147b5cf7abfa1a1c6d2cd9d3e1f21fa2a9f0975d063705f3db1e5bca354</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nicaragua-challenges-german-arms-exports-to-israel-at-icj/a-79148044--315737afbbdd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nicaragua-challenges-german-arms-exports-to-israel-at-icj/a-79148044?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany has asked the International Court of Justice to dismiss the case on jurisdiction grounds. It also said its arms exports to Israel were documented, published, and subject to more stringent checks than most.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>AfD wants to form a government in Saxony-Anhalt — but how?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7e6e13a2fae22a75cccd2a3151c051860c74262f3c1df9aa487bda91bff24bcf</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T16:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-the-afd-form-a-government-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79107331--72d013c68919.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-wants-to-form-a-government-in-saxony-anhalt-but-how/a-79107331?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following its record election success, the far-right Alternative for Germany aims to form a government. What options does it have without the absolute majority?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Beethoven Festival evokes a sense of home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c777745376a259b01095507fe728c3ed333df3f05fffb31ca46cc